---
/**
 * Audio Alive privacy policy → /audio-alive/privacy/.
 * Keep in sync with the app: permissions come from the merged manifest, events from
 * AudioAlive/app/src/main/java/com/audioalive/Analytics.kt.
 */
import AliveLayout from './_AliveLayout.astro';
import Icon from './_Icon.astro';
import { APP } from './_content';

const UPDATED = 'November 6, 2026';
const UPDATED_ISO = '2026-11-06';

const title = 'Privacy Policy — Audio Alive';
const description =
  'How the Audio Alive Android app handles data: no audio is recorded, no account is needed, and anonymous usage statistics are collected with Google Firebase Analytics.';

const site = Astro.site!;
const pageUrl = new URL('/audio-alive/privacy/', site).href;
const appUrl = new URL('/audio-alive/', site).href;

const jsonLd = [
  {
    '@type': 'WebPage',
    '@id': `${pageUrl}#webpage`,
    url: pageUrl,
    name: title,
    description,
    inLanguage: 'en',
    dateModified: UPDATED_ISO,
    about: { '@type': 'MobileApplication', '@id': `${appUrl}#app`, name: APP.name },
    breadcrumb: {
      '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
      itemListElement: [
        { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Apps', item: new URL('/', site).href },
        { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: APP.name, item: appUrl },
        { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 3, name: 'Privacy Policy', item: pageUrl },
      ],
    },
  },
];

const permissions = [
  ['FOREGROUND_SERVICE, FOREGROUND_SERVICE_MEDIA_PLAYBACK', 'Keeps the keep-alive tone playing while the app is in the background.'],
  ['POST_NOTIFICATIONS', 'Shows the ongoing notification Android requires for a foreground service, with a "Turn off" button.'],
  ['REQUEST_IGNORE_BATTERY_OPTIMIZATIONS', 'Lets you exempt the app from battery optimisation so the system does not stop it.'],
  ['INTERNET, ACCESS_NETWORK_STATE', 'Used only by Firebase Analytics to send anonymous usage statistics. The audio feature works offline.'],
  ['WAKE_LOCK', 'Added by Firebase Analytics so statistics can be sent reliably.'],
  ['AD_ID, ACCESS_ADSERVICES_AD_ID, ACCESS_ADSERVICES_ATTRIBUTION', 'Added by Firebase Analytics. Allows it to read the Android advertising ID for analytics. The app shows no ads.'],
  ['BIND_GET_INSTALL_REFERRER_SERVICE', 'Added by Firebase Analytics to learn which store page an install came from.'],
];
---

<AliveLayout title={title} description={description} jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <nav class="top" aria-label="Main">
    <a href="/audio-alive/" class="brand">
      <img src={APP.icon128} alt="" width="40" height="40" />
      <span>{APP.name}</span>
    </a>
  </nav>

  <main class="card policy">
    <header class="policy-header">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="meta">
        Last updated: <time datetime={UPDATED_ISO}>{UPDATED}</time> · Applies to the {APP.name} Android app
        (<code>{APP.packageId}</code>)
      </p>
    </header>

    <p class="tldr">
      <strong>In short:</strong> Audio Alive never records or listens to your audio, needs no account and asks for no
      personal details. It sends anonymous usage statistics to Google Firebase Analytics so we can see which features and
      dongles are used and improve the app.
    </p>

    <p>
      This policy explains what information the <strong>{APP.name}</strong> app ("the app", "we") collects, why, and the
      choices you have. The app is developed by <strong>{APP.developer}</strong>, an independent developer.
    </p>

    <h2>1. Information we do not collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>No audio.</strong> The app only plays a tone. It has no microphone permission and cannot record, read or
        analyse what you listen to.
      </li>
      <li><strong>No account, name, email, phone number or contacts.</strong></li>
      <li><strong>No precise location, photos, files or messages.</strong></li>
    </ul>

    <h2>2. Information collected automatically</h2>
    <p>
      The app uses <strong>Google Firebase Analytics</strong>. It collects the following, which is not linked to your
      name or contact details:
    </p>
    <h3>App events we log</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><code>keepalive_toggle</code>: when you turn the app on or off, and whether from the app or the notification.</li>
      <li><code>setting_changed</code>: the amplitude or frequency value you choose.</li>
      <li>
        <code>stream_started</code>: when a USB audio device connects, including its product name as reported by Android
        (for example "AB13X USB Audio") and your amplitude and frequency settings.
      </li>
      <li><code>stream_ended</code>: when the device disconnects or the app stops, and how long it was connected.</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>Collected by Firebase automatically</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>App instance ID (a random ID created when the app is installed) and, if available, the Android advertising ID.</li>
      <li>Device model, Android version, app version, language and screen resolution.</li>
      <li>Approximate country or city, estimated from your IP address. Google Analytics does not store IP addresses.</li>
      <li>Standard events such as first open, session start and app updates.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>3. How we use this information</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>To learn which USB dongles people use, so we can choose better default settings.</li>
      <li>To understand how the app is used and which features to improve.</li>
      <li>To spot problems, for example a dongle that disconnects unexpectedly.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We do not sell your information, use it for advertising, or share it with anyone except as described here.</p>

    <h2>4. Third-party services</h2>
    <p>
      Firebase Analytics is provided by Google LLC, which processes this data on our behalf. Its handling is described in
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google's Privacy Policy</a> and
      <a href="https://firebase.google.com/support/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Privacy and Security in Firebase</a
      >. Data may be processed on Google servers outside your country.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Data retention</h2>
    <p>
      Analytics data is kept in Google Analytics for no longer than 14 months and then deleted automatically. Nothing is
      stored on our own servers.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Your choices</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Reset or delete your advertising ID</strong> in Android Settings → Privacy → Ads. This stops it from being
        linked to past data.
      </li>
      <li><strong>Uninstall the app</strong> to stop all collection immediately.</li>
      <li>
        <strong>Ask for deletion</strong> by emailing us. Because the data is anonymous, include the approximate date you
        installed the app and your phone model so we can try to find it.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>7. Permissions the app uses</h2>
    <ul>
      {
        permissions.map(([name, why]) => (
          <li>
            <code>{name}</code>: {why}
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>

    <h2>8. Security</h2>
    <p>Data sent to Firebase is encrypted in transit with HTTPS. The app stores its settings only on your device.</p>

    <h2>9. Children's privacy</h2>
    <p>
      The app is not directed at children under 13 and we do not knowingly collect information from them. If you
      believe a child has used the app and want their data removed, contact us.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      If we change how the app handles data, we will update this page and the "Last updated" date above.
    </p>

    <h2>11. Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about this policy or your data: <a href={`mailto:${APP.email}`}>{APP.email}</a>
    </p>

    <a href="/audio-alive/" class="back-link"><Icon name="arrow" size={18} /> Back to {APP.name}</a>
  </main>
</AliveLayout>
